  "id": "cox-regression-analysis",
  "term": "Cox regression analysis",
  "definition": "Cox regression analysis is a statistical method used to test how individual factors are associated with prognosis, especially survival outcomes. In this context, it was used to screen genes linked to differences in survival and help build a prognostic model.",
